      "doctor_question": "Looking back at your life, have you always struggled with organizing your tasks and staying focused in this way, or is this something that has only started happening more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, dear. Well... I suppose if I am being completely honest with you—and I do want to give you all the right information—it isn't exactly a new problem. It's a little shameful to admit at my age, but... even way back when I was just a little girl, my teachers used to write on my report cards that I was a bright student. Which was very kind of them to say! But... well, they also wrote that I was a bit careless. \n\nI was always forgetting my reading books or leaving my homework behind at the house, and they constantly had to remind me to finish my seatwork before I could go outside to play. I always meant to do it right the first time, I really did. I just... lost track of myself, I suppose. \n\nI hope that doesn't make me sound like I was a bad child. I always tried to be good and polite for my teachers. Is it helpful for you to know about things from that far back, Doctor?",
